TEXT 1344 -408 Left 2 !.param Rp=5.1k\n.param Cadd1=1p\n.param Cadd2=1p\n \n; One 1-second simulated button hold after ENV has charged.\nVBTN BTN 0 PULSE(0 5 6 1m 1m 1 15)\n.model SWMOD SW(Ron=0.1 Roff=1G Vt=2 Vh=0)\n \n; Approximate red LED model.\n.model DRED D(Is=2e-20 N=2 Rs=10)\n \n.options method=gear gmin=1n cshunt=1p\n.tran 0 12 0 20u startup\n.ic V(O1)=4.8 V(O2)=0.2\n \n.meas tran Inormal RMS I(RBUZ) FROM 5.2 TO 5.7\n.meas tran Iheld RMS I(RBUZ) FROM 6.7 TO 6.9\n.meas tran Irecovered RMS I(RBUZ) FROM 11.2 TO 11.5\n \n.meas tran Tnormal TRIG V(O1) VAL=2.5 RISE=1 TD=5 TARG V(O1) VAL=2.5 RISE=2 TD=5\n.meas tran Theld TRIG V(O1) VAL=2.5 RISE=1 TD=6.7 TARG V(O1) VAL=2.5 RISE=2 TD=6.7\n.meas tran Fnormal PARAM 1/Tnormal\n.meas tran Fheld PARAM 1/Theld\n.meas tran PitchShiftPct PARAM 100*(Fheld-Fnormal)/Fnormal
TEXT 1344 280 Left 2 ;; FILT is the low-pass oscillator output and feeds Q3's input.\n; Q3 isolates the oscillator from the buzzer driver; Q5 switches buzzer current.\n \n; ENV is normally high, turning Q4 on and completing Q5's emitter return path.\n; Holding the button discharges ENV through R12, reducing Q4 current and muting the buzzer.\n; Q4 has a 100-ohm emitter resistor for a less abrupt electrical transition.\n \n; C6 is three 100 uF electrolytics in parallel: 300 uF total.\n; All C6 positive terminals connect to ENV; all negative terminals connect to ground.\n \n; ENV also drives a red LED through a 10k resistor to ground.\n; The LED visually shows ENV falling while held and recharging after release.\n \n; The simulated button is held from 6 s to 7 s.\n; Generic transistor and LED models validate circuit behavior, not exact PN2222 gain,\n; exact LED brightness, or buzzer loudness.
